            <ArticleTitle>Recurrent dislocations of the hip in a child presenting as nocturnal pains.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>470-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nocturnal pains of the leg were the only complaint of a 2 1/2-year-old girl with recurrent dislocations of the left hip. Unusual movement during sleep probably caused the dislocations. This case represents a benign entity characterized by spontaneous or voluntary posterior dislocations of the femoral head in young children without other significant connective tissue abnormalities.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
